# This tenant's app host SSH host key, pinned.
#
# The deploy step runs with `StrictHostKeyChecking=yes` against this file. It
# presents a private key that can pin an image into this tenant's Compose slot
# and restart it, so an unpinned deploy hands that key to anything that can win
# a race for the address.
#
# `ssh-keyscan` must NOT be used to fill this in: it is trust-on-first-use, and
# recording whatever answered defeats the point of pinning. The value comes from
# the host itself, over the operator's own root session:
#
#   ssh -i ~/.ssh/id_ed25519_hetzner root@<app-host-public-ipv4> \
#     'cat /etc/ssh/ssh_host_ed25519_key.pub'
#
# Then write one line here: the host's public address (the same value as the
# APP_HOST_SSH_ADDRESS repository variable), a space, and that whole line.
#
# CI refuses to deploy while this file carries no key line. It is committed
# rather than held as a secret because a host public key is not one -- publishing
# it is what pinning means.
